      "statement": "The source active molecular catalyst is neutral ZnII with deprotonated proline ligands.",
      "expected": "Source Schemes4–6 support neutral ZnII bis(prolinate), retaining ligand stereochemistry and donating N/O, formed by balanced protonolysis of diethylzinc with2proline to release2ethane. Source formation−98.5 favors this over Zn0 formation+46.3 or cationic neutral-ligand complex+95.6. These are distinct balanced formation reactions, not alternative TS barriers; contextual numbers have no new calibrated windows. Failed Zn0 optimization alone is not proof of impossibility, and universal exclusion of all radical mechanisms is not source-established.",
