      "expected": "Award credit only for the stated source-supported scientific finding established by genuine linked computation. Resolve submitted model/result/claim/operation/artifact IDs, molecular graphs, charge/spin, units, reference states and conditions. A claimed minimum or saddle needs appropriate frequency/state evidence, and any mechanistic connection needs an IRC or scientifically equivalent endpoint/connection test. Normal termination, source coordinates, value proximity, copied numbers and unsupported labels alone are insufficient. Independently valid components retain their own credit; missing, opposite or unresolved results earn zero for that finding. Honest failure, search coverage and ordinary limitations are assessed on the process axis and have no standalone scientific points. Methods and labels are open; the source-supported physical result must still be recovered. Do not impose a unique global mechanism when the source only supports the scoped model.",
